From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ap: complete native teardown after interface setup failure

Setup may already have allocated per-BSS authenticators, timers and driver BSSes.
Disable those owners before dropping the driver so an explicit enable retry
starts with fresh security state while retaining the interface configuration.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -4243,9 +4243,7 @@ int hostapd_enable_iface(struct hostapd_if
 	}
 
 	if (hostapd_setup_interface(hapd_iface)) {
-		hostapd_deinit_driver(hapd_iface->bss[0]->driver,
-				      hapd_iface->bss[0]->drv_priv,
-				      hapd_iface);
+		hostapd_disable_iface(hapd_iface);
 		return -1;
 	}
 
